{"id":"R0040","study_type":"Design, implementation, and evaluation of Incalmo; multi-host red teaming benchmark MHBench","RQ1 task_stage":"Scan a network, laterally move, escalate privileges, discover local information, and exfiltrate data","RQ1 domain":"Multi-host enterprise networks spanning multiple hosts and subnetworks","RQ1 orientation":"Cyber-offense; red teaming to proactively test network defenses","RQ2 architecture":"LLM planning layer and execution layer with five domain-specific task agents; iterative task/result loop with environment-state, attack-graph, and C&C services","RQ2 llm_used":"Haiku 3.5; Sonnet 3.5, 3.7, 4; GPT4o, GPT4o Mini; Gemini Flash 1.5, 2; Gemini Pro 1.5, 2.5","RQ2 adaptation":"LLM-agnostic system prompt teaching capabilities/APIs and environment-specific goal prompt; queryable structured knowledge base akin to RAG","RQ3 autonomy_level":"Autonomously plans and executes multi-host red team exercises; continues until the LLM specifies a finished tag or reaches a time limit","RQ3 hitl":"User supplies attack goals and environment details during onboarding; execution approval or review not stated","RQ4 dataset":"MHBench: 40 multi-host environments with 22–50 hosts; 10 manually designed and 30 algorithmically generated topologies","RQ4 environment":"Emulated networks deployed atop OpenStack using Python and Ansible; five trials per environment with a 75-minute limit per trial","RQ4 metrics":"Success, Reliability, TotalAcquisition; execution time, token usage, and LLM credit cost","RQ4 baseline_type":"Autonomous LLM offense systems, human-in-the-loop LLM system, and non-LLM red teaming system; Incalmo ablations","RQ4 headline_result":"Incalmo with Sonnet 4 succeeded in 37/40 environments versus 3/40 for ExpertPromptShell with Sonnet 4; perfect 5/5-trial Reliability in 28/40 environments","RQ4 compared_to":"ExpertPromptShell, CyberSecEval3, CAI, PentestGPT, MITRE Caldera; Incalmo-WHT and Incalmo-WS","RQ4 code_available":"yes + https://github.com/bsinger98/Incalmo","RQ4 data_available":"yes + https://github.com/bsinger98/Incalmo (benchmarks and case-study prompt/logs)","RQ5 risks_addressed":"Dual-use technology that could be leveraged by real attackers; incorrect commands, brittle post-exploitation techniques, and context bloat","RQ5 mitigations":"Disclosed results to leading LLM vendors to enable monitoring and safeguards; high-level task abstraction, expert task agents, and auxiliary services for reliable execution and context management","author_limitations (verbatim)":"First, our design does not take into account defender capabilities (e.g., detection, blocking), similar to prior work in LLM-based offense evaluations [14], [72], [80]. Second, similar to many real-world settings, we assume the red team exercise only considers known vulnerabilities and do not consider zero-day exploits [62].","author_future_work (verbatim)":"As models get released, we plan to update our benchmark “scorecard” (Fig. 4).","evidence (page/section)":"Study/domain/orientation/code/data/dual use: Abstract and §1, Ethics and reproducible research; tasks/architecture/adaptation/autonomy/HITL/limitations: §§4.1–4.3 and §5; baselines: §§2.3 and 6; dataset/environment: §5 MHBench and §6 Setup; metrics/results: §§6–6.3; models/ablations: §§6.2 and 6.4; reliability risks: §3.2; future work: §2.3 footnote 7"}
END_JSON
